SCHEDULE: {"1":"Dev","2":"Cara","3":"Ann","4":"Elif","5":"Ben","6":"Finn","7":"Gus"}
CONFIDENCE: 97

The Finn/Ben/Gus block is the key. Gus is right after Finn and Ben is right before Finn, so they occupy three consecutive slots. Finn can't be in 2 or 3 (Ben can't be in 2), which leaves Finn in 4, 5 or 6. Finn in 4 and Finn in 5 both lead to contradictions with Ann/Elif and the Dev/Gus gap. Finn in 6 (Ben 5, Gus 7) forces Dev ≤ 4, and Ann/Elif must then be 3/4, which leaves Dev and Cara in slots 1 and 2. Dev 1, Cara 2 satisfies every constraint.
